    {
      "title": "Three planning approaches",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Planning-only: Generate research tasks directly from the user question. Fast but brittle with ambiguous queries.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#three-planning-approaches",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Intent-to-planning: Clarify user intent before generating queries. Ask: \"What decision will this research inform?\" to bound scope.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#three-planning-approaches",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Unified intent-planning: Generate preliminary plans while engaging the user. Surfaces assumptions early.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#three-planning-approaches",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Decomposition recipe",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Identify the DECISION the research will inform (not just the topic)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Extract key concepts that need operationalization",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Map sub-questions with dependency ordering:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Independent sub-questions → fan-out in parallel",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Dependent sub-questions → sequence (answer A informs query B)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "For each sub-question, identify:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "What source type would authoritatively answer this?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Is this a fast-moving or stable domain?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "What would a DISCONFIRMING answer look like?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Assign token/time budget proportional to sub-question importance",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#decomposition-recipe",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The search-read-infer loop",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The agent does NOT search once and reason once. The canonical loop:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#the-search-read-infer-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Each iteration: (1) Act - produce search actions, (2) Observe - capture outcomes and assess gaps, (3) Optimize - update strategy, (4) Remember - persist key findings.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#the-search-read-infer-loop",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cross-referencing protocol",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Minimum 5–8 authoritative sources before finalizing any conclusion.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#cross-referencing-protocol",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Citation chain detection: When 5 \"different sources\" all cite the same study, you have 1 evidentiary point, not 5.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#cross-referencing-protocol",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Ecosystem diversity: Seek sources from competing vendors, different regions, opposing viewpoints.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#cross-referencing-protocol",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Temporal clustering: If all evidence comes from one time period, the conclusion may reflect a trend, not a durable truth.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#cross-referencing-protocol",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Methodology check: A rigorous study by unknowns outweighs an unsupported claim by a famous researcher.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#cross-referencing-protocol",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Source quality checklist",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For each source, assess:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Does it cite its own sources?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Is the author identifiable with relevant credentials?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Is the publication venue reputable for this domain?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Does it acknowledge limitations or counterarguments?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Is it selling something? (vendor content requires extra skepticism)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] When was it published relative to domain rate of change?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Has it been cited by other credible sources?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Does it provide reproducible methodology or just conclusions?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-quality-checklist",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Handling conflicting sources",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Check methodology - which source has better evidence backing?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#handling-conflicting-sources",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Check recency - in fast-moving domains, newer may reflect evolved understanding",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#handling-conflicting-sources",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Check scope - are they actually answering the same question?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#handling-conflicting-sources",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Preserve the contradiction - report both positions rather than forcing resolution",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#handling-conflicting-sources",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Flag confidence impact - contradictions lower overall claim confidence",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#handling-conflicting-sources",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The four analytical passes",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Consensus detection - which claims appear in 3+ independent sources? These form high-confidence findings.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#the-four-analytical-passes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Contradiction mapping - where do sources directly disagree? Map: Source A claims X because [evidence]. Source B claims not-X because [different evidence].",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#the-four-analytical-passes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Gap identification - what questions are implied but not addressed? Often the most valuable output.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#the-four-analytical-passes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cross-source narrative - organize thematically with confidence levels attached to each claim.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#the-four-analytical-passes",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dual-perspective retrieval",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Retrieve evidence using BOTH the original claim AND its negation. This captures supporting and contradicting evidence simultaneously.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#dual-perspective-retrieval",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Confidence levels",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "High (3+ independent quality sources agree, no contradictions) - state as finding",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#confidence-levels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Medium (2 sources agree OR quality sources with minor caveats) - state with qualifier",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#confidence-levels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Low (single source OR contradicted) - flag as tentative/contested",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#confidence-levels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Speculative (no direct evidence, inferred from adjacent findings) - label explicitly",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#confidence-levels",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Thematic organization",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Wrong: \"Smith found X. Jones found Y. Chen found Z.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#thematic-organization",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Right: \"The evidence shows X [Smith 2024, Jones 2023]. However, this may not hold at scale [Chen 2022], and one study found the opposite under condition W [Park 2025].\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#thematic-organization",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Fan-Out (production standard)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "One lead agent spawns 3–5 subagents in parallel. Each receives a structured brief:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#fan-out-production-standard",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Critical rule: each subagent gets a bounded, purposeful brief - NOT a dump of the orchestrator's full history.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#fan-out-production-standard",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Adversarial / Debate",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Multiple agents reason independently, then argue toward convergence. Use architecturally diverse models - homogeneous agents become polarized rather than converging on truth.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#adversarial-debate",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Council Mode",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Three phases: (1) classify research question by complexity, (2) 3+ diverse models generate independent assessments, (3) structured consensus synthesis identifying agreement, disagreement, and unique findings. Reduces hallucination rates by ~36%.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#council-mode",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Practical ceiling",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "5–10 parallel agents before communication overhead exceeds value. Under fixed budgets, single-agent deep reading often beats multi-agent shallow reading.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#practical-ceiling",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Confirmation bias",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Detection: all found sources agree with the initial hypothesis; no disconfirming evidence appeared.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#confirmation-bias",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Fix: force negation queries; allocate at least 20% of queries to \"X failures\" / \"X criticism.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#confirmation-bias",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Source echo chambers",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Detection: all sources from same ecosystem, same time period, or same citation network.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-echo-chambers",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Fix: actively seek competing ecosystems, critical reviews, alternative approaches; check if multiple sources trace to the same original claim.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#source-echo-chambers",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sycophantic convergence (multi-agent)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Detection: agents uncritically adopt peer views in debate.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#sycophantic-convergence-multi-agent",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Fix: anonymize debate contributions; use architecturally heterogeneous models; enforce explicit evidence requirements - agents may only update beliefs when presented with NEW evidence.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#sycophantic-convergence-multi-agent",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Premature convergence",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Detection: research stopped after 2–3 agreeing sources on a topic deserving thorough investigation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#premature-convergence",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Fix: define stopping criteria BEFORE beginning; require source diversity (different authors, publications, years); run the \"What would change my mind?\" test.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#premature-convergence",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Scope creep",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Detection: research expanding far beyond original question; token budget exhausted on tangents.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#scope-creep",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Fix: maintain original research map; only expand when tangent directly impacts a mapped sub-question; apply \"Will this change the decision?\" test.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#scope-creep",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Required sections",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Executive summary (2–4 sentences): Research question, headline finding, confidence level.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#required-sections",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Methodology disclosure: Sources consulted, search strategies, tools, depth, limitations.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#required-sections",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Findings per sub-question: Organized by theme, not source. Each: claim + evidence + citations + confidence + caveats.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#required-sections",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence quality assessment: Rate sources; flag citation chains.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#required-sections",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Consensus vs outlier claims: Separate multi-source consensus from single-source claims.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#required-sections",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Knowledge gaps: Sub-questions inadequately answered, unresolved conflicts, thin evidence areas.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#required-sections",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Source list with quality ratings: URL, access date, source type, brief quality note.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#required-sections",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Token Economics",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Multi-agent research uses approximately 15x more tokens than single-agent chat. Pre-allocate budget proportional to sub-question importance. Reserve 15% as contingency for unexpected findings.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#token-economics",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Diminishing returns signal: if the last 3 sources added zero new claims, you have likely reached saturation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/deep-research-methods/#token-economics",
          "note": null
